Report a connection that Schannel sees closed in the middle of a record.
When the peer closed the connection while part of a TLS record was still
waiting to be decrypted, tls_read treated it like a clean end of the
session: the partial record was dropped without a word and ssl_client
exited with status 0, so a reply cut short in transit looked complete.
Die with "truncated TLS record" instead, as the internal TLS code does.
A close at a record boundary without close_notify is still accepted as
the end of the data, also like the internal TLS code.

---
 networking/tls.c |    2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

--- a/networking/tls.c
+++ b/networking/tls.c
@@ -3340,6 +3340,8 @@
 						state->in_buffer + state->in_buffer_offset,
 						sizeof(state->in_buffer) - state->in_buffer_offset);
 					if (result == 0) {
+						if (state->in_buffer_offset != 0)
+							bb_error_msg_and_die("schannel: truncated TLS record");
 						state->connection_state = BB_SCHANNEL_CLOSED;
 						goto Success;
 					} else if (result < 0) {
